course: dictionary
lesson: 1647
title: A tall word with smoke in it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chimney is a tall pipe that carries smoke and hot gases from a fire up and out through the roof. The words around it give clues: «smoke goes up the chimney» tells you where the smoke travels.
explain: Read this: «Swifts scream over the chimneys in summer.» Swifts are birds that fly high, so the chimneys must be tall things sticking up above the roofs. Try the swap: "Swifts scream over the tall pipes in summer" still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A chimney can be the whole pipe, or just the part that sticks up above the roof. Read the sentence around the word to see which meaning the writer means.
fact: A chimney is a tall pipe or structure that carries smoke and hot gases from a fire or stove up and out through the roof.
fact: «Chimney» can also mean the part of the pipe that sticks up above the roof.
fact: Soot can catch fire, so chimneys must be cleaned.
fact: «Some African termite mounds» have chimneys and tunnels that let air move in and out, built by insects only a few millimetres long.
fact: Phrases with chimney include «chimney sweep», «chimney pot» and «smoke like a chimney».
exercise: What is a chimney? | A kind of bird that flies over roofs | A hole in the ground for water | *A tall pipe that carries smoke and hot gases up and out through the roof | A small room where you cook food
exercise: «Some African termite mounds have chimneys and tunnels for air.» What are the chimneys for? | Storing soil for the winter | Hiding food from birds | Playing music for the insects | *Letting air move in and out
exercise: Why must chimneys be cleaned? | *Because soot can catch fire | Because they need new paint every day | Because Father Christmas uses them | Because birds leave crumbs inside them
test: Which thing does a chimney carry up through the roof? | Rain and snow | Coal and bread | Birds and stones | *Smoke and hot gases
test: «...the minerals turn into black smoke and build tall chimneys.» What kind of thing is a chimney here? | A type of fish | A small green plant | *A tall pipe-like structure | A soft blanket
exam: Why does smoke go up the chimney? | Because the chimney is a bird's nest | Smoke likes to sit at the bottom of the fire | *Hot gas rises, and the chimney carries it up and out through the roof | Because the roof pulls it down into the room
